      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "This is the medical/healing なおす, written with {治|なお}す. It means to cure illness or heal injury, as opposed to {直|なお}す which means to fix or repair broken objects or mistakes. Both are read なおす but use different kanji.\n\nCONTRAST WITH {直|なお}す:\n- {治|なお}す — to cure/heal (illness, injury)\n- {直|なお}す — to fix/repair (broken objects, mistakes)\n\nINTRANSITIVE PAIR:\n- {治|なお}す (transitive) — someone cures something\n- {治|なお}る (intransitive) — something heals/gets better on its own\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {病気|びょうき}を{治|なお}す — to cure an illness\n- {怪我|けが}を{治|なお}す — to heal an injury\n- {虫歯|むしば}を{治|なお}す — to treat a cavity\n- {風邪|かぜ}を{治|なお}す — to cure a cold",
